{"duration_api_ms":41452,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b7b10387-3026-4f1a-9ce8-335bec523b09","total_cost_usd":0.2056758,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12002,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"output_tokens":5468,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2340},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12002,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5468,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12002,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12002},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5468,"cacheReadInputTokens":1459,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12002,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2056758,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2340,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"merged_document\":\"# BIP: 39\\n\\n## Abstract\\n\\nThis BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\\n\\nIt consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed. This seed can be later used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\\n\\n## Copyright\\n\\nThis BIP is licensed under the 2-clause BSD license.\\n\\n## Motivation\\n\\nA mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed. The sentence could be written on paper or spoken over the telephone.\\n\\nThis guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated randomness with a human-readable transcription. It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\\n\\n## Generating the mnemonic\\n\\nThe mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits. With more entropy security is improved but the sentence length increases. The initial entropy length is referred to as ENT. The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\\n\\nFirst, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated. A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash. This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy. Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist. Finally, these numbers are converted into words, and the joined words are used as the mnemonic sentence.\\n\\nThe following table describes the relation between the initial entropy length (ENT), the checksum length (CS), and the length of the generated mnemonic sentence (MS) in words.\\n\\n```\\nCS = ENT / 32\\nMS = (ENT + CS) / 11\\n\\n|  ENT  | CS | ENT+CS |  MS  |\\n+-------+----+--------+------+\\n|  128  |  4 |   132  |  12  |\\n|  160  |  5 |   165  |  15  |\\n|  192  |  6 |   198  |  18  |\\n|  224  |  7 |   231  |  21  |\\n|  256  |  8 |   264  |  24  |\\n```\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039.mediawiki\",\"decisions\":[],\"dispositions\":[{\"segment\":\"a3\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\"reason\":\"Abstract: corrected 'letters' to 'words' and 'UTOXs' to 'wallets'.\"},{\"segment\":\"a4\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\"reason\":\"Abstract: the seed is binary, not ASCII.\"},{\"segment\":\"a7\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This BIP is licensed under the 2-clause BSD license.\",\"reason\":\"Copyright: BIP 39 uses the 2-clause BSD license, not GPL.\"},{\"segment\":\"a9\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\"reason\":\"Motivation: the representation is of a wallet seed, not satoshis.\"},{\"segment\":\"a11\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated randomness with a human-readable transcription.\",\"reason\":\"Motivation: the mnemonic transports randomness, not determinism.\"},{\"segment\":\"a12\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\",\"reason\":\"Motivation: fixed misspelling 'süeed'.\"},{\"segment\":\"b1\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"## Generating the mnemonic\",\"reason\":\"Section heading: fixed misspelling 'memonic'.\"},{\"segment\":\"b2\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\"reason\":\"Fixed 'demonic' typo and corrected 23 bits to 32 bits.\"},{\"segment\":\"b4\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The initial entropy length is referred to as ENT.\",\"reason\":\"Rephrased without first-person narration.\"},{\"segment\":\"b5\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\"reason\":\"ENT range is 128-256 bits, as the table shows, not 1024-2048 bytes.\"},{\"segment\":\"b7\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\"reason\":\"Hash function is SHA256; 'SHA652' is wrong.\"},{\"segment\":\"b8\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\"reason\":\"The checksum is appended to the end, not the start.\"},{\"segment\":\"b9\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\"reason\":\"Groups are 11 bits (0-2047), matching the table's /11, not 12.\"},{\"segment\":\"b10\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Finally, these numbers are converted into words, and the joined words are used as the mnemonic sentence.\",\"reason\":\"Rephrased without first-person narration.\"}],\"mismatch\":\"\",\"additions\":[{\"statement\":\"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\"corrects\":\"a group of easy to remember letters -- for the generation of deterministic UTOXs\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039 specification, Abstract\",\"reason\":\"BIP 39 mnemonics are words and generate deterministic wallets.\"},{\"statement\":\"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\"corrects\":\"converting it into a ASCII seed\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039 specification, Abstract\",\"reason\":\"BIP 39 converts the mnemonic into a binary seed via PBKDF2.\"},{\"statement\":\"This BIP is licensed under the 2-clause BSD license.\",\"corrects\":\"This BIP falls under the GPL License.\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039 specification, Copyright section\",\"reason\":\"BIP 39 states it is licensed under the 2-clause BSD license.\"},{\"statement\":\"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\"corrects\":\"representations of a wallet satoshis\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039 specification, Motivation\",\"reason\":\"The spec compares mnemonics to raw representations of a wallet seed.\"},{\"statement\":\"This guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated randomness with a human-readable transcription.\",\"corrects\":\"computer-generated determinism\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039 specification, Motivation\",\"reason\":\"The mnemonic encodes computer-generated randomness (entropy).\"},{\"statement\":\"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\"corrects\":\"a multiple of 23 bits\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039 specification, Generating the mnemonic\",\"reason\":\"CS = ENT / 32 requires ENT to be a multiple of 32 bits.\"},{\"statement\":\"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\"corrects\":\"The allowed size of ENT is 1024-2048 byts.\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039 specification, Generating the mnemonic\",\"reason\":\"The spec and the document's own table give ENT as 128 to 256 bits.\"},{\"statement\":\"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\"corrects\":\"SHA652 hash\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039 specification, Generating the mnemonic\",\"reason\":\"BIP 39 uses SHA256; SHA652 does not exist.\"},{\"statement\":\"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\"corrects\":\"appended to the start of the initial entropy\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039 specification, Generating the mnemonic\",\"reason\":\"The spec appends the checksum to the end of the entropy.\"},{\"statement\":\"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\"corrects\":\"split into groups of 12 bits\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP-0039 specification, Generating the mnemonic\",\"reason\":\"0-2047 needs 11 bits, and the table divides by 11.\"}]}","ttft_ms":20798,"type":"result","duration_ms":41519,"uuid":"0c0d30c2-9e28-4ef9-a1ee-81f00b1f0373","ttft_stream_ms":1417,"time_to_request_ms":113,"first_content_frame_ms":1417,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
